# 🚀 DSA Visualizer

An interactive web-based Data Structures and Algorithms Visualizer built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

This project helps students understand how common data structures and algorithms work through real-time visual animations, complexity analysis, and interactive controls.

---

## ✨ Features

### 📦 Data Structures

* Array Operations

  * Insert Element
  * Delete Element

* Stack

  * Push
  * Pop
  * Stack Visualization

* Queue

  * Enqueue
  * Dequeue
  * Front / Rear Indicators

---

### 🔍 Searching Algorithms

#### Linear Search

* Step-by-step visualization
* Element comparison tracking
* Complexity display

#### Binary Search

* Low, Mid, High pointers
* Search space elimination
* Sorted array visualization
* O(log n) demonstration

---

### 🔄 Sorting Algorithms

#### Bubble Sort

* Element comparisons
* Swap animations
* Progressive sorting visualization

#### Selection Sort

* Minimum element tracking
* Boundary visualization
* Swap demonstration

#### Insertion Sort

* Key element tracking
* Element shifting animation
* Sorted section visualization

---

## 📊 Complexity Analysis

Every algorithm includes:

* Time Complexity
* Space Complexity

Examples:

| Algorithm      | Time Complexity |
| -------------- | --------------- |
| Linear Search  | O(n)            |
| Binary Search  | O(log n)        |
| Bubble Sort    | O(n²)           |
| Selection Sort | O(n²)           |
| Insertion Sort | O(n²)           |

---

## ⚡ Animation Controls

Users can control visualization speed:

* 0.5x
* 1x
* 2x

This makes learning easier by allowing slower or faster execution.

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used

* HTML5
* CSS3
* JavaScript (ES6)
* DOM Manipulation
* Async/Await
* Event Handling

